9132       data multi;
9133       input Prep $ Dose Symptoms $ N;
9134       LDose=log10(Dose);
9135       if Prep='test' then PrepDose=LDose;
9136       else PrepDose=0;
9137       datalines;

NOTE: The data set WORK.MULTI has 24 observations and 6 variables.

9162       ;
9163       proc probit data=multi;
9164       class Prep;
9165       nonpara: model Symptoms(order=data)=Prep LDose PrepDose / lackfit;
9166       weight N;
9167       run;

NOTE: PROC PROBIT is modeling the probabilities of levels of Symptoms having LOWER Ordered Values in the response profile table.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: The LACKFIT option is ignored since the AGGREGATE (or AGGREGATE=) option was not specified for the multinomial model.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE PROBIT printed page 611.

